  "prefLabel": "Env-Or 503.03 Throughput Recordkeeping Required",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Or 503.03 Throughput Recordkeeping Required. The owner or operator of a gasoline storage tank having a capacity equal to or greater than 250 gallons shall:\n\n(a) Record daily gasoline throughput volume;\n\n(b) Maintain the records required by (a), above, for not less than 3 years; and\n\n(c) Make such records available for inspection and copying upon written request by the department or the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA).\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Or 500) #10229, eff 11-17-12; ss by #13458, eff 10-7-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-or500.html"
